WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.355
Hi, I'm Painter!

00:00:02.355 --> 00:00:06.617
Nanbeige four point three is a thirty-three billion parameter model, released first

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:08.748
so it can teach smaller ones.

00:00:08.748 --> 00:00:10.169
Let's open it up.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:15.834
Build the strongest agent you can first, then use it to teach small models.

00:00:15.834 --> 00:00:17.257
The teacher is out now.

00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:18.395
The student is not.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.012
A token goes up through fifty-two identical blocks.

00:00:25.012 --> 00:00:27.647
No experts, no loops, no sliding windows.

00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.600
The feed-forward layer holds about four fifths of every block's weights.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.178
Seven query heads share each key and value head, so only

00:00:35.178 --> 00:00:36.327
eight heads are cached.

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:39.328
But every layer keeps a cache.

00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:43.272
That is two hundred eight kilobytes a token, over three times Qwen's hybrid.

00:00:43.272 --> 00:00:46.608
At long context the cache, not the weights, is the bill.

00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.499
The chat template shows how it acts.

00:00:50.499 --> 00:00:53.303
It thinks first, then names a function in XML.

00:00:53.303 --> 00:00:55.485
Results come back as a user turn.

00:00:55.905 --> 00:00:57.212
Think inside think tags.

00:00:58.614 --> 00:00:59.579
Name the function.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.489
Give each parameter a tag.

00:01:04.031 --> 00:01:05.960
Results return as a user turn.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.573
A base model goes through post-training.

00:01:10.573 --> 00:01:14.082
The recipe, the data and the environments are not published.

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:17.634
Out comes the thirty-three billion teacher, with open weights.

00:01:18.054 --> 00:01:20.710
It is then meant to teach a three billion student.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.304
How, the team has not said.

00:01:23.925 --> 00:01:28.449
The card reports it leading on seventeen of twenty benchmarks against three rivals.

00:01:28.449 --> 00:01:30.536
Those are the publisher's own runs.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.729
A teacher is a claim about the future.

00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:35.608
The cache is a bill you pay today.

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:43.282
To recap: a plain dense model, a heavy cache, and a teacher

00:01:43.282 --> 00:01:44.761
whose student has not arrived.

00:01:45.181 --> 00:01:47.264
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.264 --> 00:01:47.859
I'm Painter.

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:48.157
Bye!
